---
// OVER-40 TRAINING PAGE (doc 74 §2). Long-tail phrase "personal trainer over
// 40 / 50 / 60"; non-geo title, Denver in the body.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StickyBook from '../../components/StickyBook.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';
import { REVIEWS, REVIEWS_URL } from '../../data/reviews';

import hero from '../../assets/training/rings.jpg';

const title = 'Personal Trainer for Over 40, 50 and 60 | Jamie Atlas';
const description =
  'One-on-one strength training in downtown Denver for adults over 40, 50 and 60 with a knee, back or shoulder that has a history. Build muscle at any age. $57 assessment, studio or Zoom.';

const susan = REVIEWS.find(r => r.name === 'Susan Keicher');

const faq = [
  { q: 'Is it too late to build muscle at 60?', a: 'No. Muscle responds to load at every age; what changes is how much recovery the program has to respect. Susan started here in her sixties having never trained. Results vary from person to person, but the direction doesn\'t.' },
  { q: 'Do I need to be fit before I start?', a: 'No. The first visit is an assessment of where you are, not a test you can fail. The program starts from what your body accepts today.' },
  { q: 'What if I\'ve got a bad knee?', a: 'That is most of who I train. The program is built around the joint you\'re worried about, with someone in the room who can tell a muscle that\'s working from a joint that\'s complaining.' },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map(f => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
};

const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Strength training over 40, 50 and 60',
  serviceType: 'Personal training',
  provider: { '@id': SITE.url },
  areaServed: { '@type': 'City', name: 'Denver' },
  url: `${SITE.url}/personal-trainer-denver/over-40`,
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', name: '30-minute assessment (first visit)', price: '57', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} image="/studio-coaching.jpg">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(serviceSchema)} />

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-14 pb-10 md:pt-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_.9fr] gap-10 items-center">
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif italic text-[var(--color-primary)] mb-3 text-lg">Strength over 40</p>
        <h1 class="mb-6">Build muscle at any age. Keep the joints you came in with.</h1>
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Somewhere after 40 the advice changes from "train hard" to "be sensible", and nobody says out loud what
          "sensible" costs you. Muscle you don't use goes. Bone follows it. Balance goes last, without announcing
          itself, and by then the stairs have an opinion.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <a href="/book" class="cta-button text-lg">Book a 30-minute assessment</a>
          <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">{SITE.pricing.firstVisit}, in the studio or on Zoom</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-primary)]">
          {SITE.awardBadge} · 9NEWS fitness expert · {SITE.contact.address.street}, downtown Denver
        </p>
      </div>
      <Image
        src={hero}
        alt="A client over 40 training on gymnastic rings at Jamie Atlas's downtown Denver studio"
        widths={[640, 1000]}
        sizes="(min-width: 768px) 45vw, 100vw"
        format="webp"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] w-full h-auto max-h-[560px] object-cover object-top"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BODY -->
  <section class="px-6 py-12 bg-[var(--color-surface)] border-y border-[var(--color-border)]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-lg text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text)] font-semibold text-xl">The body over 40 still builds muscle. It just stops forgiving bad programming.</p>

      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-[var(--color-primary)] mb-2 pt-4">What changes after 40</h2>
      <p>
        Recovery takes longer, so the program has to respect the day after, not just the session. Old injuries are now
        part of the anatomy: the meniscus from 2009, the shoulder from the crash, the back that goes when it feels like
        it. And the price of a bad week is higher, because a strain at 55 costs six weeks, not six days.
      </p>
      <p>
        None of that is a reason to train less. It's a reason to have someone in the room who can tell the difference
        between a muscle that's working and a joint that's complaining.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-[var(--color-primary)] mb-2 pt-6">What I do differently</h2>
      <p>
        I'm a personal trainer with a rehab specialist's eye. Every program here is built around the joint you're
        worried about, not despite it. Cognitive Functional Therapy tells me what your pain system will accept this
        week. Applied Functional Science tells me where the load should go. Then we lift, in the studio or on Zoom, at
        weights that go up.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nutrition coaching is in the fee, because protein is the part of the over-40 equation most people get wrong,
        and it's the cheapest thing to fix. If you're on a GLP-1 medication,
        <a href="/personal-trainer-denver/glp-1">there's a page for that</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-[var(--color-primary)] mb-2 pt-6">Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        You're 40, 50, 60 or past it. You ski, golf, hike, run, or you used to. You've never lifted, or you lifted in
        your twenties and the body you're in now doesn't remember. You have at least one joint with a story. You don't
        want a gym; you want a program and a person.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-[var(--color-primary)] mb-2 pt-6">How a session runs</h2>
      <p>
        First visit, a 30-minute assessment, {SITE.pricing.firstVisit}. I watch you move, find the one change that
        helps most, and you feel it before you leave. Then 60 minutes or 30, one-on-one, {SITE.pricing.session60} or
        {SITE.pricing.session30}, same price in the studio at {SITE.contact.address.street} or online. The 6:30am and
        5:15pm slots are open most weeks.
      </p>

      {susan && (
        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[var(--color-primary)] pl-5 py-1 text-base italic">
          "{susan.text}"
          <footer class="not-italic text-sm mt-2 font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">{susan.name}, <a href={REVIEWS_URL} rel="noopener">on Google</a></footer>
        </blockquote>
      )}

      <p>
        Tom, 68, came in on pain medication and left it behind after four months. That's one person; results vary from
        person to person. But it's the kind of thing that happens here often enough that I stopped being surprised.
      </p>

      <p class="text-[var(--color-text)] font-semibold pt-4">
        Bottom line: the best time to start lifting was twenty years ago. The second best time is before the next
        thing goes.
      </p>

      <p class="text-base pt-2">
        <a href="/what-i-work-with/masters-athlete-injuries">Recurring injuries after 40, in detail →</a> ·
        <a href="/for">By activity: skiers, golfers, runners and more →</a> ·
        <a href="/personal-trainer-denver/glp-1">Training on a GLP-1 →</a> ·
        <a href="/personal-trainer-denver">Personal training in downtown Denver →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="px-6 py-14">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="mb-6">Questions people over 40 ask</h2>
      <div>
        {faq.map((f, i) => (
          <details open={i === 0} class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)] py-4 last:border-b">
            <summary class="font-serif font-bold text-xl cursor-pointer">{f.q}</summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">{f.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FINAL CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 bg-[var(--color-primary)] text-on-dark">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <h2 class="mb-6 text-white">Thirty minutes. One measurable change. Then you decide.</h2>
      <p class="text-xl mb-10 opacity-95">
        A 30-minute assessment, {SITE.pricing.firstVisit}, in the studio or on Zoom. If it's not a fit I'll say so in the
        first half hour, and I'll know who is.
      </p>
      <a href="/book" class="cta-button cta-button-accent text-lg">Book a 30-minute assessment</a>
      <p class="mt-8 text-sm opacity-80">
        {SITE.contact.address.street}, {SITE.contact.address.level} · <a href={`tel:${SITE.contact.phoneTel}`} class="text-white underline">{SITE.contact.phone}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <StickyBook />
</BaseLayout>
